implementationPlan.description:
Worktree-mode test rows SR-T5 and SR-T5-replay in scripts/tests/postflight-vm-route.sh [strong receipt].
After SR-T4 add:
`vmr_run SR-T5 worker codex "$SG_READY" on 0 "${SG_STRONG[@]}" FAKE_CHECK_DISPATCH=pass FAKE_EVIDENCE_MODE=receipt-conflict-finalize-lost`, then `sr_check SR-T5 lost`.
Then save the project (`rm -rf "$TMP_DIR/sr-keep"; cp -a "$PROJECT" "$TMP_DIR/sr-keep"`) and set VMR_SETUP=sr_restore (reuse T2's). Run `vmr_run SR-T5-replay worker codex "$SG_READY" on 0 "${SG_STRONG[@]}" FAKE_CLAIM_MODE=finalizing FAKE_EVIDENCE_MODE=receipt-conflict`, set VMR_SETUP=sg_fixture again, then `sr_check SR-T5-replay lost-replay`.
Update both section echo lines to T1-T5. The closing line must read `[strong receipt] ok T1, T2, T2-replay, T3, T4, T5, T5-replay`, because checkRefs[0] greps it on every engine.
New sr_check kinds:
- lost (the live worktree landing: a receipt conflict, then every finalize lost):
  - the prelude as today; rec.length 1, rec[0] deepEqual want, and the completion row before it;
  - exactly one conflict line;
  - fin.length 3 (one exhausted finalize), each outcome landed with landedRevision C, and rec[0] before fin[0];
  - phase finalizing, and deferred 0;
  - exactly one line that starts with '[WARN] receipt journal ' and ends with ' kept: its completion row, delivery receipt or closed attempt is not recorded yet; the next pre-flight replays it.';
  - exactly one '[WARN] finalize_attempt acknowledgement exhausted; stopping new-task loop (no repeated Git effect).' line;
  - the journal still on disk with exactly T2's strong keys and fields: move T2's key and field asserts into one small function both kinds call, rather than copying them;
  - no .moe/receipts/<id>.json.
- lost-replay (the next pre-flight: a conflict again, the finalize answered):
  - rec.length 2, and JSON.stringify(rec[1].args) === JSON.stringify(rec[0].args);
  - exactly one conflict line and one '[receipt] replaying the delivery receipt of task task-postflight from ' line;
  - fin.length 4. The last one is landed with landedRevision C, comes after the last receipt, and has attemptId, generation and workerId equal to fin[0]'s;
  - phase closed, the journal gone, kept 0 and deferred 0;
  - check-dispatch and record_candidate rows 1 each (nothing re-dispatched or re-frozen), and no stored receipt.
Also extend the conflict-line count to ['conflict','lost','lost-replay'], and skip the stored-receipt pushResult check for both lost kinds (a conflict stores nothing). The SR-T1..T4 assertions stay as they are. Test first: on today's wrapper SR-T5 must fail on the missing journal (a full `bash postflight-vm-route.sh` takes about 6 min).
